# width: 120
# height: 40
# The launcher dock's edge grip (src/ui/edge_grip.zig) under the default
# `ui.dock.placement = .inner`: `⋯` at the middle of the row the strip
# paints — the editor area's last row, above the statusline, cells
# 58..60 with the glyph on 59 at 120 columns. The items appear where the
# grip is, never apart from it: hover, click and keyboard all bring the
# strip up on row 37, and the `:` line's row 39 keeps its own job.
#
# `edge_grip_dock_outer.test` is the other placement, where grip and
# strip are both on the `:` line's row and the line has to take it back.
#
# The bar and the columns ship `.always`, so the only grip on this
# screen is the dock's.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
# `auto_hide`, as mnml ships: nothing is drawn, and the grip says where.
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"
# The `:` line's row is the line's, middle and all: a click on 59 39
# opens it rather than pinning anything.
click 59 39
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
expect screen lacks "dock pinned"
key esc
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"
# Dwelling on the grip reveals the strip, because the grip is INSIDE
# the dock's hover zone and not a second way in.
hover 59 37
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
# Away: the strip goes and the grip comes back.
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"
# Resting on the `:` line's row summons nothing now.
hover 59 39
wait 600
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
hover 60 10
wait 300

# ── an open `:` line leaves the grip alone ──
# Grip and strip are above the statusline and cover nothing of the
# line, so the grip stays up while the line takes keys, and the dwell
# still brings the strip out.
key ctrl+;
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
expect screen contains "⋯"
hover 59 37
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
key esc
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"

# ── a click on the grip pins, and never opens the `:` line ──
click 59 37
expect screen contains "dock pinned"
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect screen lacks "⋯"

# ── pinned, the strip is still row 37 and the `:` line two rows below ──
# A click on row 39 opens the line; one on the strip's own row 37 does
# not, which is the proof of where each of them is.
click 110 39
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
key esc
click 100 37
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"

# Unpinning hands the strip back to `ui.dock.mode`, and the grip with it.
command view.dock_pin
expect screen contains "dock: auto_hide"
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"

# ── the keyboard: `view.focus_dock` brings it up on the same row ──
# The `:` line's row still answers for itself while the keys are in the
# strip, and a click on row 37 lands on the strip's own items (column
# 78 is New terminal's word — `launcher_dock_always.test` has the
# arithmetic): the proof that the items came up where the grip was.
command view.focus_dock
expect screen contains "New terminal"
click 78 37
wait 900
expect pane Terminal
